#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0046 expect=violation domain=SUPPAE
#note "BOUNDARY the twin cannot reach -- pins 'flags the MINORITY', not 'flags everything'. The AESOSP group now has a STRICT MAJORITY (2 vs 1): rows 1 and 2 agree on 'Other Medically Important SAE', row 3 alone carries 'Other Serious Event'. flagInconsistentGroupMinority flags ONLY row 3 -- the count is 1, not 3. The adapted invalid-SUPPAE fixture is the 1-vs-1 tie where every non-blank row is flagged; together the two pin both halves of D.2. NEUTER CHECK: delete row 2 and the group becomes a tie and the count becomes 2."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 QNAM=AESOSP QLABEL="Other Serious Event"
dataset SUPPAE label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP  | Other Medically Important SAE | Y | CRF
S1 | AE | 002 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP  | Other Medically Important SAE | Y | CRF
S1 | AE | 003 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP  | Other Serious Event           | Y | CRF
S1 | AE | 001 | AESEQ | 2 | AETRTEM | Treatment Emergent Flag       | Y | DERIVED
